# Normally, Docker's data root is something like: /var/lib/docker  # depending on the Docker storage driver/configuration.
      - Where does Docker physically store the images/data?	
		> docker info --format '{{.DockerRootDir}}'
# useful command 
		> docker system df # it show also volumes

        - Volumes are persistent storage.For example, your database containers may have volumes containing database data.
	- Check them with:
		> docker volume ls
	then :	> docker volume inspect <volume-name> # That will show where the volume lives.		
